{
  "about": "Shared vectors for the wire envelope (RFC wire-signing, packages/contracts/src/wire-signing.ts). The keys are RFC 8032 §7.1 TEST 1 (router) and TEST 2 (platform): published test keys, never used anywhere but here. A verifier in another language rebuilds each canonical text from its input, checks the signature under the signer's public key, and checks that the kid is base64url of the first 8 bytes of SHA-256 over the raw public key. Each entry of invalid must be refused, for the reason given, when verified at its now against these keys and its expected values (a call with replay none); each entry of invalidKeyLists must be refused when the key lists are loaded. Both versions are here: an entry whose input has v 2 is substrat-wire/2 (K-66), eighteen lines with the caller app, caller scope and actor after the vertical line; every other entry is version 1. A verifier accepts both. A person actor is person: and the SHA-256 hex of the onBehalf token's UTF-8, which the receiver recomputes from the token it is handed. The version 2 row a router call carries (a caller, or the platform actor) is judged against the expected target, and refused as caller when it is the other row.",
